/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - Statement.
   - Why it works.
   - Statement.
   - Vth = INRth, Rth = Voc/Isc
   - Vth in volts, IN = Isc in amperes, Rth = RN in ohms.
   - This is source transformation applied to the whole network: a voltage source in series with R becomes a current source V/R in parallel with the same R.
   - A dependent source cannot be switched off and cannot be merged into a resistance, so series-parallel reduction fails.
   - With dependent sources Rth can come out smaller than any single resistor, or even negative, which means the network can deliver power from its controlled source.
   - Answer.
*/
